  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 242 PM CDT Wed Sep 9 2026\n\nFriday...Most models in good agreement of migrating both sfc and \nupper ridging off to the east enough to allow some warming return \nflow acrs the region. Most areas should recover back up into at \nleast the lower 80s with sunshine. This while upper level troffiness \norganizes acrs the northern plains into the upper MS RVR Valley \nalong with underlying sfc frontogenesis for storm development acrs \nmuch of MN into the mid MO RVR Valley by Friday night. With the \ncurrent progressive looking nature of the developing cold front, \nthere may be a chance for some of this convection to bleed down into \nthe local area late Friday night into Sat morning, if in a weakening \nfashion.\n\nSaturday through Tuesday...The above mentioned front may be pushing \nout of the CWA by early SAt afternoon, making any showers and storms \nscooped up by this FROPA occurring more in the morning to midday and \nnot the most optimum time for strong to severe storms. Pre-frontal \nwarm and moist draw will make for a bit warmer and humid day with \nhighs in the mid 80s to near 90 and sfc DPTs pooling in the upper \n60s to around 70, but much will depend on frontal timing and these \nwarmer conditions may occur acrs more of the southeast half of the \nDVN CWA, while areas from DBQ and CID and west stay in the 70s for \nambient temps. Amounts of cloud cover and convective debris could \nalso be a temp limiting factor.\n\nA passing post-frontal ridge may then produce a short precip lull \nSaturday night into Sunday before signs of a more significant \ndigging short wave or upper low acrs the northern plains amplifies \nsteering cyclonic southwesterly flow toward the upper midwest and \nnorthwestern GRT LKS.  May have to watch for convection with \nassociated warm frontal retreat through the region Sunday night, \nplacing the local area in a breezy warm sector for Monday with highs \nin the upper 80s to around 90. Heat indices may range from 95 to 100 \nagain if low to mid 70 sfc DPTs can advect up this way. Thus local \nheat while a MCS or two impact the northern plains acrs to the heart \nof the GRT LKS like a deep summer style pattern. An eventual cold \nfrontal push off the passing wave to the north, may bring some \nstorm activity further southward into the local area either Monday \nnight or into Tuesday, before we can count on a cooling post-frontal \nairmass and heat reprieve into the mid next week period.",
